  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    if rows == 0:\n        return []\n    \n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    if cols == 0:\n        return [[] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Extract the sequence of colors from outside to inside\n    layers = []\n    \n    # Start with the full grid\n    r1, c1 = 0, 0\n    r2, c2 = rows - 1, cols - 1\n    \n    # Get the outermost color\n    current_color = grid[r1][c1]\n    layers.append(current_color)\n    \n    while True:\n        # Find bounding box of cells with different color inside current bounds\n        new_r1, new_c1 = r2, c2\n        new_r2, new_c2 = r1, c1\n        found = False\n        \n        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n            for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                if grid[r][c] != current_color:\n                    found = True\n                    if r < new_r1:\n                        new_r1 = r\n                    if c < new_c1:\n                        new_c1 = c\n                    if r > new_r2:\n                        new_r2 = r\n                    if c > new_c2:\n                        new_c2 = c\n        \n        if not found:\n            break\n        \n        # Move to the inner rectangle\n        r1, c1 = new_r1, new_c1\n        r2, c2 = new_r2, new_c2\n        current_color = grid[r1][c1]\n        layers.append(current_color)\n    \n    # Create the output grid\n    k = len(layers)\n    size = 2 * k - 1\n    result = [[0 for _ in range(size)] for _ in range(size)]\n    \n    for i in range(size):\n        for j in range(size):\n            # Distance from the nearest edge\n            d = min(i, j, size - 1 - i, size - 1 - j)\n            result[i][j] = layers[d]\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    if rows == 0:\n        return []\n    \n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    if cols == 0:\n        return [[] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Extract the sequence of colors from outside to inside\n    layers = []\n    \n    # Start with the full grid\n    r1, c1 = 0, 0\n    r2, c2 = rows - 1, cols - 1\n    \n    # Get the outermost color\n    current_color = grid[r1][c1]\n    layers.append(current_color)\n    \n    while True:\n        # Find bounding box of cells with different color inside current bounds\n        new_r1, new_c1 = r2, c2\n        new_r2, new_c2 = r1, c1\n        found = False\n        \n        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n            for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                if grid[r][c] != current_color:\n                    found = True\n                    if r < new_r1:\n                        new_r1 = r\n                    if c < new_c1:\n                        new_c1 = c\n                    if r > new_r2:\n                        new_r2 = r\n                    if c > new_c2:\n                        new_c2 = c\n        \n        if not found:\n            break\n        \n        # Move to the inner rectangle\n        r1, c1 = new_r1, new_c1\n        r2, c2 = new_r2, new_c2\n        current_color = grid[r1][c1]\n        layers.append(current_color)\n    \n    # Create the output grid\n    k = len(layers)\n    size = 2 * k - 1\n    result = [[0 for _ in range(size)] for _ in range(size)]\n    \n    for i in range(size):\n        for j in range(size):\n            # Distance from the nearest edge\n            d = min(i, j, size - 1 - i, size - 1 - j)\n            result[i][j] = layers[d]\n    \n    return result",
